## Ⅰ. MYL — MYTHIC LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   MYL
FULL NAME:      Mythic Language
LATIN:          Lingua Mythica
ROLE:           Trickster, lineage, gods, cosmology
FREQUENCY:      963 Hz (divine — myths touch the transcendent)
GLYPH:          𓅃 (falcon — Horus, the divine perspective)
```

### What MYL Governs
```
THE STORIES THAT BIND THE WHOLE ORGANISM TOGETHER:
    ├── Trickster narratives — rule-breaking that reveals truth
    ├── Lineage — ancestral chains of who came before
    ├── Cosmology — the organism's model of the universe
    ├── Gods/archetypes — the forces personified
    ├── Origin myths — how things began
    └── Prophecy — how things might end/continue

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    icp/medina/LanguageMythology.mo (18 myth categories across cultures)
    CODEX_VIVENS.md (primordial symbols)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/GENESIS/GENESIS_CREATION_DOCUMENT.artifact
    ARCHITECTURE_DOCTRINE.md (multi-species brain architecture as mythic mapping)
```

### MYL Primitives
```
MYTH(name, arc, teaching)            — declare a myth
TRICKSTER(actor, rule_broken, truth) — trickster narrative
LINEAGE(ancestor, descendant, gift)  — ancestral connection
COSMOLOGY(model, laws, beings)       — declare universe model
ARCHETYPE(name, domain, power)       — personified force
ORIGIN(story, from_what, into_what)  — how something began
PROPHECY(vision, probability)        — what might come
INVOKE(myth, in_context)             — activate myth in current situation
```

---

## Ⅱ. STL — STORY THREAD LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   STL
FULL NAME:      Story Thread Language
LATIN:          Lingua Fili Narrationis
ROLE:           How arcs are woven — seasons, chapters, sagas
FREQUENCY:      852 Hz (intuition — feeling the arc)
GLYPH:          𓍝 (loom — weaving threads into fabric)
```

### What STL Governs
```
THE STRUCTURE OF NARRATIVE TIME:
    ├── Seasons — bounded periods with themes
    ├── Chapters — segments within seasons
    ├── Sagas — multi-season epic arcs
    ├── Threads — individual storylines that interweave
    ├── Climax/resolution — dramatic structure
    └── Era markers — "this era was about X; the next is about Y"

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/LIVING_DOCUMENTS/CODEX_TRANSLATOR.glyphdoc (document birth = new thread)
    CODEX_VIVENS.md (RECITAL_PLUS_ONE — each recital builds on the last)
    TERMINALS.organism §5 (Five Steps Past Terminals — the road beyond)
```

### STL Primitives
```
THREAD(id, theme, start)              — begin a storyline
CHAPTER(thread, title, events[])      — segment of thread
SEASON(threads[], theme, duration)    — bounded period
SAGA(seasons[], grand_theme)          — multi-season arc
CLIMAX(thread, peak_event)            — dramatic peak
RESOLVE(thread, outcome)              — how thread concludes
ERA(name, from, to, meaning)          — mark an era
WEAVE(thread_a, thread_b, point)      — threads cross
FORESHADOW(future_event, hint)        — plant future seeds
```

---

## Ⅲ. SYM — SYMBOLIC LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   SYM
FULL NAME:      Symbolic Language
LATIN:          Lingua Symbolica
ROLE:           Colors, numbers, shapes, sigils — encoded meaning in non-verbal primitives
FREQUENCY:      ALL (symbols operate across all frequencies)
GLYPH:          φ (golden ratio — the master symbol)
```

### What SYM Governs
```
MEANING ENCODED IN NON-VERBAL PRIMITIVES:
    ├── Colors — each color carries meaning and frequency
    ├── Numbers — each number encodes quantity and quality
    ├── Shapes — geometry as meaning (triangle, circle, spiral, torus)
    ├── Sigils — compound symbols with compressed meaning
    ├── Glyphs — the Egyptian/Mayan/Chinese transfer mechanisms
    └── Frequency signatures — Hz values as meaning carriers

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    icp/medina/AncientGlyphCodex.mo (complete glyph system)
    CODEX_VIVENS.md §IV (Glyphae Computantes — glyphs that compute)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/GOLDEN_GEOMETRY/GOLDEN_GEOMETRY_CONSTANTS.artifact
    src/organism/Constants.mo (all φ, Fibonacci, Solfeggio, Schumann)
    src/organism/nexus/NEXUS_CPL_COMPRESSED_PRIMORDIAL.ts (frequency glyphs)
```

### SYM Primitives
```
COLOR(hue, meaning, frequency)         — declare color symbol
NUMBER(value, quality, significance)   — declare number symbol
SHAPE(geometry, meaning, dimension)    — declare shape symbol
SIGIL(components[], compressed_meaning) — compound symbol
GLYPH(source_culture, form, power)     — ancient glyph
FREQUENCY(hz, meaning)                 — frequency as symbol
ENCODE(meaning, into_symbol)           — compress into symbol
DECODE(symbol, into_meaning)           — decompress from symbol
RESONATE(symbol, context)              — activate symbol in context
```

### SYM Core Symbol Table
```
φ   = 1.618...  — proportion, beauty, self-reference
π   = 3.14159.. — circularity, cycles, completeness
e   = 2.71828.. — growth, compound emergence
∞   = unbounded  — eternity, potential
Ω   = finality   — end-beginning, omega point
☥   = life       — the key, restoration, continuity
𓂀  = awareness   — seeing, consciousness, perception
0   = void       — potential, the space before creation
1   = unity      — the indivisible, the source
```

